= Result

This round did *not* build a secure PKE. It proposed and independently evaluated two materially different interfaces. M1, LABELLED-NORM-HOM-LIFT, remains a construction gap: its Hom-lattice lift, complete norm-fiber enumeration, fiber-correctness bound, and attacker-to-complete-EndRing extractor are absent. M2, simultaneous full-module conjugation, is rejected for the submitted syntax: public linear algebra recovers the normalized conjugator used by its mask.

Novelty, QPT/QROM security, a correct-direction reduction to complete EndRing, and NIST Category 5 remain *unestablished*. No parameter set was selected. Scientific, implementation, formalizer, benchmark, and parameter-selection runs were all zero.

