= M1 — LABELLED-NORM-HOM-LIFT

== Proposed syntax

For a public supersingular curve E over the quadratic field, public basis (P,Q) of the L-torsion, and M dividing L, encryption samples r, sets a=m+Mr and the cyclic kernel generated by P+[a]Q, and emits the j-invariant of the quotient. The public sender needs no ring. The intended private operation would use a complete evaluable rank-four basis of End(E) to construct all of Hom(E,C), enumerate all norm-L maps, and recover one residue modulo M.

== Reviewed gaps

Correctness is exact only conditionally: if F(c) is the set of labels reaching c, the reference decoder returns m exactly when every a in F(c) has residue m modulo M. No negligible cross-message fiber bound is supplied.

Knowing End(E) does not itself give a connecting map, a complete Hom(E,C) basis, principalization, or bounded norm enumeration. The exact reference decoder publicly enumerates all L labels, so polynomial L supplies no recipient asymmetry. A single norm-L Hom witness reveals at most one label and is not a complete-ring separator.

The required reduction must map a successful QPT labelled-quotient distinguisher to a complete evaluable saturated basis of End(E). No exact-law challenge simulator, extractor, loss, or adaptive-OneEnd bridge is supplied. O1–O6 remain open. M1 is a construction gap, not a PKE or impossibility theorem.

= M2 — simultaneous full-module conjugation

== Proposed syntax

Public U,V generate the full two-by-two matrix algebra over Fℓ. The sender samples an invertible matrix S, publishes its simultaneous conjugates X and Y, and masks m with a hash of the normalized projective class N(S).

== Public recovery

Solve the public equations XT=TU and YT=TV. For an honest transcript write T=SC. Then C commutes with U and V. Their generated algebra is the full matrix algebra, whose centralizer is scalar, so the solution space is exactly the scalar multiples of S. Every nonzero solution has the same normalization N(S).

A classical passive adversary, hence also a valid QPT adversary, recovers the exact hash input. One ordinary hash query and zero decryption queries recover the selected message. For distinct challenge messages the advantage is 1/2. Conditional actual-message correctness is discharged, but it is public correctness; O4 is contradicted for this syntax. An integral lift cannot hide a pad already fixed by public matrices.

